course: dictionary
lesson: 15722
title: Words for being lost in thought
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A trance is a state where you are awake but do not notice what is around you. Your mind has gone somewhere else. Read the words around trance to find its meaning. «Mia sat staring at the rain, in a trance, and did not hear her name.» She was awake, but she noticed nothing. Trance means a state like dreaming.
explain: The clues here are staring and did not hear her name. Someone can also be in a trance when they are lost in music, thought or wonder. «The crowd was in a trance as the singer played her last song.» Nobody moved or talked, because everyone was caught up in the music.
explain: Stories often use this word. «The Rat and the Mole heard the wonderful piping and fell into a trance of awe.» Trance means the animals were so amazed they forgot everything else. To check, swap in «lost in wonder» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A trance is a state where you are awake but do not notice what is around you.
fact: «In a trance» means not paying attention to what is happening around you.
fact: «Fall into a trance» means to become suddenly lost in a dream, a thought or a wonder.
fact: A trance can be deep thought, music or wonder, not only sleep.
fact: Trance music is a kind of fast electronic dance music.
exercise: «Mia sat staring at the rain, in a trance, and did not hear her name.» What does in a trance mean? | Asleep in bed at night | Shouting loudly | *Lost in thought, not noticing what is around | Running very fast
exercise: «The crowd was in a trance as the singer played her last song.» What does trance suggest? | Angry with the singer | Bored and leaving the hall | *Deeply caught up in the music | Cold and wet
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «fall into a trance»? | Jump up and shout | Fall over on the floor | *Suddenly become lost in a dream or wonder | Sing a loud song
test: «The Rat and the Mole heard the piping and fell into a trance of awe.» Why were they in a trance? | They were angry and wanted to fight | They were hungry and went to find food | They were bored of the music | *They were amazed and forgot everything else
test: Which word could replace trance in «He stood in a trance by the window»? | Sneeze | Shout | Race | *Daydream
exam: Ben says a trance only happens when you are fast asleep. Is he right? | No, it is a kind of food | Yes, and it always lasts all night | *No, you can be awake and lost in thought | Yes, only sleep counts
